Builds a template from a Dockerfile and a build context (default: the
current directory), streaming the build log. The gateway builds it with
BuildKit in an isolated builder, adds the Anona runtime (envd), pushes it and
registers it; sandboxes then start from it by name:

  anona-compute template build -f Dockerfile --name my-env
  anona-compute create -t my-env

--cpu, --memory and --disk size every sandbox started from the template:

  anona-compute template build --name big --cpu 4 --memory 8192 --disk 20480

The disk defaults to 1024 MiB. Your plan caps it, and a build that asks for
more is refused with the plan's limit before anything is uploaded.

Every FROM image is pinned by digest. EXPOSE 49983 (envd) is refused. The
image's CMD runs at sandbox start only when the last stage declares CMD or
ENTRYPOINT, or with --start-cmd. .dockerignore in the context is honored.

Usage:
  anona-compute template build [CONTEXT_DIR] [flags]

Flags:
      --cpu int            minimum vCPUs sandboxes from this template need, 1-8 (default 2); a sandbox can use any size that meets it
      --disk int           minimum writable disk sandboxes from this template need, 1024-81920 MiB, up to your plan's limit (default 1024)
  -f, --file string        Dockerfile (default CONTEXT_DIR/Dockerfile)
  -h, --help               help for build
      --memory int         minimum memory sandboxes from this template need, 128-16384 MiB (default 2048)
  -n, --name string        template name (default: the context directory's name)
      --no-cache           build without the build cache
      --start-cmd string   command to run when a sandbox starts (after envd)
      --tag stringArray    tag for this build (repeatable)
      --wait               stream the build log and wait until it is ready (--wait=false returns at once) (default true)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output: one object per line on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
